# Bread to Bolsheviks: Russia, 1917
subtitle: "How a bread strike toppled three centuries of Tsars in a week, and why Lenin's small party, not the crowd, held power by October."
thumb: "band \"Two revolutions, eight months\" picture \"File:19170704 Riot on Nevsky prosp Petrograd.png\""

## Bread to Bolsheviks: Russia, 1917
style: movie
sources:
    - id: figes
      title: 'A People''s Tragedy: The Russian Revolution, 1891–1924'
      authors: Orlando Figes
      year: 1996
      finding: the February rising, dual power, Kornilov and October
    - id: smith
      title: 'Russia in Revolution: An Empire in Crisis, 1890 to 1928'
      authors: S. A. Smith
      year: 2017
      finding: war, food supply and the collapse of authority in 1917
    - id: fitzpatrick
      title: The Russian Revolution (4th edition)
      authors: Sheila Fitzpatrick
      year: 2017
      finding: why the Bolsheviks, not the Provisional Government, held power

